RetroBoot: a safe right USB-C port on the Gemini PDA (VBUS for USB devices only)

Applied by build-kernel.sh (variant rightport, on top of a72dvfs2) to gemini-nixos
6a172f5's kernel delta (GPL-2.0).

The bring-up DTS hogged GPIO94 (usb1_drvvbus, the right port's 5 V source) and GPIO72
(the SW7226 load switch to the connector) high, so the right connector sourced VBUS
all the time, into a charger too, while userspace (rb-gemini-typec) put its FUSB301A
in dual-role, where a charger attaches and turns its own VBUS on.

- DTS. The GPIO94/72 hogs are gone. A pinctrl hog on &pio drives both low (GPIO mode,
  output low) when the pin controller probes, as the vendor DWS default also does, so
  the port does not source VBUS whenever the policy driver is not running. The lane mux
  hogs (GPIO70 high, GPIO71 low: USB position) stay. &usb_cc_right (i2c0 0x25) is
  enabled with compatible "retroboot,gemini-right-port", vbus-gpios (94) and
  switch-gpios (72). The left port (i2c1 FUSB301A, BQ25896 and its GPIO107 boost gate,
  the mtu3 gadget) is untouched.
- drivers/usb/typec/gemini-right-port.c (CONFIG_TYPEC_GEMINI_RIGHT_PORT=y, built in).
  The vendor policy (gemian/gemini-linux-kernel-3.18 @ 8cfe659,
  drivers/misc/mediatek/usb_c/fusb302/usb_typec.c), made stricter. Probe requests
  GPIO72 then GPIO94 output-low before touching the chip, checks the device ID (0x12),
  and sets Modes = SOURCE (0x01, as the vendor does), so a charger (Rp) never attaches
  and never sends VBUS into the port. The chip is polled (mainline pinctrl-mt6797 has no
  EINT) every 250 ms. VBUS goes on, GPIO94 then GPIO72 (vendor order), only for a USB
  device: ATTACH, Type = sink (0x10, or 0x14 with an active cable), orientation CC1 or
  CC2, VBUSOK clear, the same on two polls. It goes off, GPIO72 then GPIO94, at once on
  anything else: detach, any other partner, VBUS seen before we drive it, an I2C error,
  Modes changed outside the driver (then restored to SOURCE), allow_source=0, suspend,
  unbind and shutdown. Modes stays SOURCE at shutdown. No charge path: the right port has
  none (Planet: the left port charges; the vendor kernel never takes power from it).
- Interface. /sys/bus/i2c/devices/0-0025/{state,vbus,regs,stats} (state: idle,
  pending, sourcing, foreign-vbus, other-partner, mode-changed, i2c-error, disabled),
  sysfs_notify on state; /sys/module/gemini_right_port/parameters/allow_source (0644),
  poll_ms (0444). Transitions are logged with dev_info (below the console loglevel).
- Test. variants/rightport/test-right-port-policy.c compiles the code between the
  rightport-policy markers unchanged (check-src.sh): scenarios, every register value
  from four policy states, and random sequences.

